wall luminance L(x) monotone ↓ in local thickness d(x), monotone ↑ in proximity to its practical;

thin walls HOT, thick slabs DENSE;  cut edges (d = d_min) = argmax L  (brightest lines in frame).

ℓ → 0 (opaque paint) ⇒ premise collapses.   [your failure condition #1]

R₂  ZONE‑SPECTRAL DISTINCTNESS  [::5]   ∀ zone z : one CONCEALED practical, CCT_z = f(function(z));

pairwise Δchroma(CCT_z, CCT_z′) > τ  ⇒ the building reads as a SECTIONED LANTERN;

interior lit ONLY from within (no external fill into rooms; no visible LED hardware).

all CCT equal ⇒ uniform glowing lump.   [your failure condition #2]

R₃  SHADOW‑SCREEN LEGIBILITY  [::4]   interior occluders sit between practical and wall ⇒ each wall is a

projection screen; silhouette contrast preserved ⟺ scattering blur σ_s(ℓ) < feature size

(glow never dissolves into a blob); figures CAUGHT MID‑ACTION; props ≥ 12; exactly ONE deep‑cut detail.

R₄  SECTION + CAMERA + DOF  [::4]   ONE clean section plane removes 2 walls + roof;

60 mm macro, three‑quarter, LOW elevation, slight up‑tilt (structure LOOMS), PERSPECTIVE (¬isometric);

